From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix division by zero in the ADC reference check of SafeSystem

checkAdcReference() divides the nominal bandgap voltage by the raw
bandgap reading. AnalogInput::get() returns a BspReturnCode that the
caller discards and leaves the output at zero when the conversion does
not complete, so a single failed conversion makes the function divide
by zero. That is undefined behaviour in a function whose result feeds a
safety monitor, and the value derived from it is used again in
checkInternalSupplies().

A raw bandgap value of zero now reports the ADC reference fault
directly, without the division, and keeps the last known reference.

The valid window of the reference voltage and its nominal value moved
into named constants with a comment saying where they come from. They
are properties of the board: the S32K148EVB ties VREFH to the 5 V rail,
so 4800 to 5200 mV is right here, but a board with a 3.3 V or an
external 4.096 V reference reports a fault on every cycle and resets
the MCU until the numbers are adapted. No change in behaviour for the
S32K148EVB.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
---
 .../safeSystem/src/safeSystem/SafeSystem.cpp  | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/executables/referenceApp/platforms/s32k148evb/safety/safeSystem/src/safeSystem/SafeSystem.cpp b/executables/referenceApp/platforms/s32k148evb/safety/safeSystem/src/safeSystem/SafeSystem.cpp
index 950acf37..93b73d2c 100644
--- a/executables/referenceApp/platforms/s32k148evb/safety/safeSystem/src/safeSystem/SafeSystem.cpp
+++ b/executables/referenceApp/platforms/s32k148evb/safety/safeSystem/src/safeSystem/SafeSystem.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,19 @@
 
 namespace safety
 {
-SafeSystem::SafeSystem() : _counter(0U), _adcRef(5000U) {}
+namespace
+{
+// The ADC reference of this board is VREFH, which the S32K148EVB ties to the 5 V rail. A board that
+// feeds VREFH from another source (3.3 V, an external 4.096 V reference) has to adapt these three
+// values, otherwise checkAdcReference() reports a fault on every cycle and the supervisor resets
+// the MCU. They are named here rather than spelled out at the comparison so that a port does not
+// have to search for them.
+constexpr uint32_t ADC_REFERENCE_NOMINAL_MV = 5000U;
+constexpr uint32_t ADC_REFERENCE_MIN_MV     = 4800U;
+constexpr uint32_t ADC_REFERENCE_MAX_MV     = 5200U;
+} // namespace
+
+SafeSystem::SafeSystem() : _counter(0U), _adcRef(ADC_REFERENCE_NOMINAL_MV) {}
 
 void SafeSystem::init()
 {
@@ -41,8 +53,16 @@ void SafeSystem::checkAdcReference(uint32_t const bandgapRawValue)
 {
     constexpr uint32_t adcMaxRaw      = 0xFFFU; // 12-bit ADC
     constexpr uint32_t bandgapVoltage = 1000U;
-    _adcRef                           = bandgapVoltage * adcMaxRaw / bandgapRawValue;
-    if ((_adcRef < 4800U) || (_adcRef > 5200U))
+    if (bandgapRawValue == 0U)
+    {
+        // AnalogInput::get() leaves the value at zero when the conversion fails, and a bandgap
+        // reading of zero is a fault of the reference path anyway. Dividing by it would be
+        // undefined behaviour, so report the fault instead and keep the last reference.
+        safety::SafeSupervisor::getInstance().adcReferenceMonitor.trigger();
+        return;
+    }
+    _adcRef = bandgapVoltage * adcMaxRaw / bandgapRawValue;
+    if ((_adcRef < ADC_REFERENCE_MIN_MV) || (_adcRef > ADC_REFERENCE_MAX_MV))
     {
         auto& supervisor = safety::SafeSupervisor::getInstance();
         supervisor.adcReferenceMonitor.trigger();
-- 
